  "blocks": [
    {
      "id": "vkkpy11",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "Introduction"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "POSDCORB acronym proposed by Luther Gulick outlines the core management functions: Planning, Organizing, Staffing, Directing, Co-ordinating, Reporting, and Budgeting.",
        "Henri Fayol formulated 14 Principles of Management, emphasizing Unity of Command, Division of Work, and Scalar Chain.",
        "Nursing staffing requirements rely on patient classification systems, bed occupancy rates, and INC norms to determine optimal nurse-patient ratios.",
        "Quality Assurance in nursing care incorporates Donabedian's framework evaluating Structure, Process, and Outcome indicators.",
        "Effective communication and conflict management are vital for maintaining team morale, safety standards, and optimal ward administration."
      ],
      "id": "ear5btd"
    },
